.DS_Store
/ios/.build
/Packages

# Build output — never commit. The root `build/` is stale Xcode `Debug-iphoneos` output:
# precompiled modules, a target graph, an 873 KB build-task store. Nothing reads it —
# `make ios` writes to `tmp/build/whoopsy-dd`, `scripts/test.sh` builds into
# `tmp/build/verify`, and the host loop uses `/ios/.build` above — so it is output that
# was being tracked by accident. Root-anchored, like the two lines above, so a future
# `ios/build` or a `backend/build` is not silently swallowed along with it.
/build

xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
.swiftpm/configuration/registries.json
.swiftpm/xcode/package.xcworkspace/contents.xcworkspacedata
.netrc
Design/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Health data — never commit. These are a real person's physiological record:
# recovery, HRV, skin temperature, blood oxygen, sleep staging, and 550 free-text
# journal notes. Paired with timestamps and a timezone they are de-anonymising.
#
# `ios/Package.swift` bundles **five** files out of `Resources/` — the three CSVs this
# pattern matches, and the two JSONs under `ZeroFasting/` and `Custom/` below — and
# `Resources/` holds no tracked file at all, so a fresh clone has no such directory and
# **will not build** until the five exist. `scripts/create-data-files.sh` writes
# placeholder versions of exactly those five and cannot overwrite a file that holds
# data; README.md §Building is the narrative version. Recipe lives there and in that
# script, not here — a second copy drifts, and the drift would be a header column
# quietly missing.
#
# The directory is named for the producer, because the CSVs in it came from WHOOP —
# `ZeroFasting/` beside it is the same arrangement for a different app's export. The
# pattern names the subdirectory and not `**`, deliberately: a bare `*.csv` under
# `Resources/` would also swallow a future resource that is not health data.
# It matches `journal_entries.csv` as well, and that is intentional rather than
# incidental: that file is the one CSV here that is *not* bundled and is read by
# nothing — no `WhoopExportFile` case, no import button — so it is health data to keep
# out of git, not a file the build wants. Do not narrow the pattern around it.
ios/Sources/Whoopsy/Data/Resources/Whoop/*

# Zero Fasting — never commit, and the whole directory rather than `*.json`: what is in
# here is one fasting app's export, seven files deep, and every one of them is the same
# person's record. `biodata.json` (599 KB across 19 top-level keys) is the source; this
# app reads `fast_data` alone, projected down to `fasts.json` (46 KB) — the fourth
# resource `Package.swift` bundles, and the one `scripts/create-data-files.sh` writes
# here as `{"fast_data": []}`.
ios/Sources/Whoopsy/Data/Resources/ZeroFasting/*

# Custom — never commit, and the whole directory rather than `*.csv`: every file in here is
# a dream journal, which makes it the most identifying thing in this repository precisely
# because nothing about it looks like data — no timestamp, no device, no measurement, just
# one person's own account of their nights. It is the one directory under `Resources/` that
# is not an app's export, which is why it is not named for a producer the way `Whoop/` and
# `ZeroFasting/` above are. `dreams.csv` is the notes file and the source of truth;
# `dreams.json` is generated from it by a generator the owner keeps outside this repository
# — not repo tooling — and is the same prose with its dates resolved, so it is ignored on
# the same rule rather than matched separately.
ios/Sources/Whoopsy/Data/Resources/Custom/*

# Mapbox credentials — never commit.
# `Mapbox.local.xcconfig` holds the PUBLIC (`pk.…`) access token, which is the only
# copy of it: at the owner's request it lives outside the tree. `ios/App/Config/Mapbox.xcconfig`
# is the committed base and carries no token — it ends with `#include? "Mapbox.local.xcconfig"`,
# the *optional* include, so a clone without this file still builds and simply gets the
# pre-feature behaviour (an empty `MBXAccessToken`, `MapboxSetup.configure()` returning
# `false`, and the route card drawing `MapKit`). Recipe in README.md §Building.
# The SECRET token (`sk.…`, `Downloads:Read`) must never be written here either —
# it is a build-time credential for SwiftPM and lives in `~/.netrc` only.
ios/App/Config/Mapbox.local.xcconfig

# Cloud sync backend — never commit.
backend/node_modules
backend/.wrangler

# Testing scratch — never commit. `tmp/` is where everything produced *while testing* goes,
# so that nothing is written outside the repo and nothing local reaches a commit:
#
#   tmp/screenshots/  simulator captures taken while verifying a change
#   tmp/scratch/      one-off probe sources and build logs
#   tmp/backups/      simulator-container SQLite copies
#   tmp/build/        build output — SwiftPM's scratch path (`scripts/test.sh`) and Xcode's
#                     derived data (`make ios`). Pure output; `make clean` removes it.
#
# The pattern is `/tmp/*` and not `/tmp/`, deliberately. Excluding the directory itself
# stops git descending into it, and the tracked README below it could then never be
# re-included — the rule is "you cannot un-ignore a file whose parent directory is ignored".
tmp/*
!tmp/README.md